WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.080
Our next guest is the mother of two and she created a line

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.410
of masks for the whole family,

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.690
and we're so happy that she did,

4
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.360
and we're so happy that she's here.

5
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.740
From supermodel to supermom,

6
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.405
please welcome Karolina Kurkova.

7
00:00:16.405 --> 00:00:18.891
(audience applauds)

8
00:00:18.891 --> 00:00:19.724
Hi.

9
00:00:19.724 --> 00:00:20.557
Hello.

10
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.210
How are you, Drew?

11
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.810
I'm really good, and I wanted to jump right in

12
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.800
by showing you two pictures of me.

13
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.800
I took them this weekend in honor of you being here,

14
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.350
and I have to tell you,

15
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.660
I have been wearing this mask nonstop.

16
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:44.070
Now, obviously nobody knew masks would be a thing this year,

17
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.316
but you and Billie Blooms have elevated them

18
00:00:46.316 --> 00:00:49.110
to not only a real fashion accessory,

19
00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.825
but every time I wear it, I feel like I'm blowing a kiss.

20
00:00:51.825 --> 00:00:55.140
It's, they're just really incredible quality

21
00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.430
and they're optimistic and beautiful.

22
00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:58.763
How did this all start?

23
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.600
Well, thank you so much for saying so many nice things

24
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.793 line:15%
about the masks.

25
00:01:03.793 --> 00:01:07.640 line:15%
Really. When we started with my friend, Ashley Liemer,

26
00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:08.767
back in early April,

27
00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.464
we really wanted to do something that was giving back

28
00:01:11.464 --> 00:01:14.891
and to our community and to people, you know,

29
00:01:14.891 --> 00:01:19.780
that were losing jobs, including Ashley's seamstresses

30
00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.910
that she's been working with for over 15 years,

31
00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.024
that, you know, suddenly she had to let go.

32
00:01:26.024 --> 00:01:29.010
And we really have, being moms,

33
00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:32.150
we knew we wanted to create masks that really were happy,

34
00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:35.610
that were fashionable, that were fun and different,

35
00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.680
and really make it a little bit more fun and easier

36
00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.820
for people to wear them, especially for children.

37
00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.307
You know, how do you tell a three-year-old,

38
00:01:42.307 --> 00:01:44.840
"Oh, now suddenly you have to wear these masks,"

39
00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.970
which you know, they're not so comfortable.

40
00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:48.745
Yes, you do get hot underneath them,

41
00:01:48.745 --> 00:01:50.414
and so we really worked really hard.

42
00:01:50.414 --> 00:01:52.140
How can we make them more comfortable?

43
00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.350
How can we make them more fun?

44
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.995
And so we did embroidery of cats and a dog,

45
00:01:55.995 --> 00:01:59.210
which is our cat, Kaja, and dog, Bowie.

46
00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.683
And we gave it also a story

47
00:02:00.683 --> 00:02:04.130
to kind of turn this mask-wearing around

48
00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:07.530
from being something that's like so hard and difficult.

49
00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:08.490
It's, you know what?

50
00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:09.720
You are a superhero,

51
00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.230
and even superheroes don't just wear capes,

52
00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.490
but they wear masks to protect the people

53
00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.470
that they love around them.

54
00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.520
Can I come join your family?

55
00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:21.040
Because you are an amazing mom.

56
00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:26.040
And that is the type of rhetoric and words, words matter.

57
00:02:26.307 --> 00:02:29.110
They are everything to me.

58
00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:34.110
And it is so unique to find a new language

59
00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:38.550
about everything this year and how we empower our kids

60
00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.720
and how we make them aware and responsible,

61
00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.130
but keep it not scary, and joyful

62
00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:48.980
is one of the most original, unique, difficult, tightropes

63
00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.910
we will ever walk in our lifetime.

64
00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:53.110
And I just have to say that I think

65
00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.823
what you are doing is profoundly important

66
00:02:55.823 --> 00:02:57.880
and they're excellent masks.

67
00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.480
I put them in the little yellow book this week.

68
00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.220
I am in love with these,

69
00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:05.759
and I'm so grateful for you to do what you are doing.

70
00:03:05.759 --> 00:03:08.220
And we here on the show really celebrate it.

71
00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.720
Thank you Karolina, for being an amazing woman,

72
00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.950
an amazing mom, and now making a product that truly works

73
00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.170
in every single way.

74
00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.520
Thank you.

75
00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.353
Thank you.

76
00:03:19.353 --> 00:03:22.040
And also, I forgot to mention that from every mask

77
00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.570
that's purchased from us, proceeds goes to Feeding America.

78
00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:27.570
And that really was really important for us,

79
00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:30.780
really just giving back and keeping families safe,

80
00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.900
and thank you, thank you.

81
00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.840
It's been really an incredible journey

82
00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.230
and to have something, you know,

83
00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:39.003 line:15%
during times where it has been so confusing

84
00:03:39.003 --> 00:03:40.070 line:15%
and you're at home,

85
00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.950 line:15%
and especially when everything started to feel so helpless,

86
00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.210 line:15%
you know, I'm not a doctor, Ashley's not a doctor.

87
00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:47.400 line:15%
We felt like we wanted to do something.

88
00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.218 line:15%
And really this project gave us so much joy and creativity

89
00:03:50.218 --> 00:03:53.600
and have our families and our children being part

90
00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.266
of creating these masks for other children and, you know,

91
00:03:56.266 --> 00:03:59.610
being our models and test models.

92
00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.213
And it's been really incredible, you know,

93
00:04:03.493 --> 00:04:05.786
and now it's our new accessory and, you know,

94
00:04:05.786 --> 00:04:10.770
keeping us safe and keeping it fun.

95
00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.550
And beautiful. Thank you, Karolina.

96
00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:13.400
Billieblooms.com.

97
00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:17.750
(happy, laidback music)

